From 6c473abf5b7dd636c9daf5b211d9c04ce9200876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:40:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: judge missing parents and unclaimed-ready
 notices only from a copy at the feed head

A sync round stuck in a long pull (2026-11-12, laptop-1 ~75k changes behind) left the
remote-parent mirror and the live board old. The missing-parent detector then blocked two
rework cards whose parents were done on the Board and filed repair cards, and the 30-min
"ready with no worker" notices reported three cards that were running or scheduled elsewhere.

New kanban_replica_freshness: the replica's mark_pulled stamp (pulled_at, written only after a
pull reaches the feed head) must be within 600 s on the same board.
- note_missing_parents (readiness txn): on a synced board an absent parent is unknown unless the
  replica is at head: no parent_missing streak event, no block, one DEBUG line
  'parent status unknown: replica not at head'. A fresh replica that lacks the parent still
  blocks and files one repair card.
- kanban_parent_unclaimed.sweep: no notice while the replica shows lag (kanban_chat_wait.sweep is
  covered by main's lag_hold, t_01a1d390d19239dd, now in the same module);
  the ready timer keeps running, so a card still unclaimed after catch-up is reported next tick.

Recurrence: hub t_01a1d2c873e82536 (18:41 PT) was the same false positive (hub mirror got the
done parent only after a delayed replica pull).
